# Patch: Kimchi compatibility fixes for pi-ai 1.3.0
#
# Tracking: none yet. No matching upstream issue exists; report these
# changes to https://github.com/earendil-works/pi before the next upgrade.
# Changes:
#   - Accept JSON-encoded array/object tool arguments (including {} as an empty
#     array) in coercePrimitiveByType.
#   - Run coerceWithJsonSchema before Value.Convert, and wrap conversion errors
#     with the received arguments so models can self-correct.
#   - Drop upstream's TYPEBOX_KIND guard so coercion also applies to
#     TypeBox-defined schemas (Kimchi's own tools are TypeBox-defined). Both the
#     guard and its then-unused declaration are removed on purpose.
#   - Count LiteLLM cache_creation_tokens as cache writes.
# Careful: validateToolArguments interleaves with upstream's
#   normalizeOptionalNulls() - keep that call first when rebasing.
# Removal: delete each hunk when the pinned Pi release provides that behavior.
# History: see patches/CHANGELOG.md.
#
